From 70f09367ff81b74ef5350cf70276725e4e58f40c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retropineaple <118107729+retropineaple@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:35:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 41/54] Restore the render engine registers before GPU hang
 replay (-wex-reset-restore)

On this GPU the hung work sits on the donor's second ring (0x1A000 block),
whose reset uses the render GDRST domain but whose restore list only names
its own 0x1A000 registers. The render engine's mode (execlists), status
page and chicken registers are cleared and never restored, so every replay
hangs again. Before a render-domain reset, wake the render domain and save
those registers from a healthy engine; after the GDRST, with the donor's
forcewake still held, write them back before work is replayed. Opt-in;
also enables the reset trace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 README.md                               |  1 +
 README_ja.md                            |  1 +
 WhateverXe/kern_xe.cpp                  | 86 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 tests/fixtures/boot_argument_names.json |  1 +
 4 files changed, 88 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

